    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d407">

                <pb facs="0566" n="550" xml:id="pg550"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.61351/2–1048: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Norweb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-02-10T13:00:00-05:00">February 10,
                            1948—1 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>169. Meeting of Cuban sugar leaders and Belt with President Grau yesterday
                    afternoon apparently agreed to sell one million tons at 4 cents which Marshall
                    reportedly accepted by phone. Important reservation, however, that army can move
                    only through deep ports still unacceptable Cuba.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Norweb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
